sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, one Swamp run, hub peers as one file per Node (orbit-peers.d), native steps because the work is under five steps (rule 22). docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#wireguard-hub.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: node:wireguard-key
  %% kind: node.wireguard_key
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant H as WireGuard hub<br/>vpn Node
  CLI->>GW: node:wireguard-key<br/>NODE PUBLIC-KEY
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:wireguard-key NODE PUBLIC-KEY`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> <public-key> [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node and its WireGuard public key, as canonical base64 of 32 bytes
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, store the key
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the target Node
  %%> - the target does not hold the `gateway` role (`node.wireguard_key_gateway`)
  %%> - the target is unmanaged: it lacks a WireGuard address or a pinned SSH host fingerprint, or both; with both it is managed (`node.wireguard_key_managed`)
  %%> - the target has a WireGuard address (`node.wireguard_ip_required`)
  %%> - the key is valid and belongs to no other Node and not to the hub (`node.wireguard_key_conflict`); the check and the assignment are atomic across concurrent assignments
  %%> - no other lifecycle change runs for the Node's name (`node.provisioning_busy`)
  %%> - no other `node:wireguard-key`, `node:converge`, add or remove runs on the Node or holds the hub (`operation.target_busy`), so an older run cannot write an old key back
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the key is stored, the change is broadcast, and a task is recorded with the full intent; the target is never contacted
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-wireguard-key
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task ID, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>H: Write the peer file<br/>cfgmgmt file
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes this peer's file in the hub's peer folder with the new key; the other peers' files stay
  SW->>H: Apply the peer<br/>SSH argv · wg set
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the previous key from the live hub and adds the new one, so the old key is not left listed
  %%> - sending the same key again repeats these steps, so a retry repairs a failed one
  SW->>H: Check the hub<br/>native assert
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the one end check: the live hub lists the peer with the new key and its allowed address, and not the previous key
  alt hub lists the peer
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the task succeeds
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Keep the stored key
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the stored key stays and the task fails with the failed step
    %%> On the hub:
    %%> - after a failed write the old file stays; after a failed apply the new file is on disk and the live hub still has the old key; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again after fixing the hub; a `node:converge` of the hub publishes the stored key too
  end
  opt run completed or failed
    SW->>SW: Remove the run folder<br/>private run files
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
